[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: learning.HOW_TO_UPDATE
class: universal
version: 1.0.0

[HOW_TO_UPDATE]
overview: Step-by-step process for updating documentation
principle: Small edits, clear commits, no breaking changes

[STEP_1_IDENTIFY]
task: Determine which file to update and what section
process:
  1. Read the discovery (rule, error, or info)
  2. Check WHEN_TO_UPDATE.toon (does it qualify?)
  3. Check WHEN_NOT_TO_UPDATE.toon (any veto?)
  4. Use FILES_REFERENCE.toon (which file?)
  5. Read target file (understand current structure)
result: Know exactly what file and where in that file

[STEP_2_LOCATE]
task: Find the exact section in target file
process:
  1. Open target file from FILES_REFERENCE.toon
  2. Read file structure (sections, format)
  3. Find matching section for info
  4. If section exists: UPDATE it
  5. If section missing: ADD at appropriate place
danger: Don't break file structure. Maintain consistent format.

[STEP_3_CHECK_DUPLICATE]
task: Ensure info isn't already documented
process:
  1. Search target file for keywords
  2. Check related files (use QUICK_LINKS.toon)
  3. If found: LINK instead of duplicate
  4. If found but outdated: UPDATE existing
  5. If new: ADD as new entry
result: No duplicate knowledge

[STEP_4_WRITE_UPDATE]
task: Compose the update
process:
  1. Keep it SHORT (5-10 lines typical)
  2. Use TOON format if in .toon file
  3. Use Markdown if in .md file
  4. Include context (why? found where?)
  5. Add reference if applicable (line number, commit)
example_good:
  [CONSTRAINT_11]
  rule: All FFI functions validate ALL pointer inputs
  why: C boundary is untrusted
  pattern: if (!ptr || !size) return STATUS_INVALID;
  source: bindings/ffi.cpp code review
example_bad:
  "FFI functions should probably validate inputs maybe"

[STEP_5_USE_EDIT_TOOL]
task: Apply the update to file
tool: Use Edit tool, not raw file modifications
process:
  1. Identify exact old_string (including context)
  2. Write exact new_string (with update)
  3. Use Edit tool (preserves formatting)
  4. Verify change was applied correctly

[STEP_6_VERIFY_CHANGE]
task: Ensure update is correct and file is valid
process:
  1. Read file section again (verify change applied)
  2. Check TOON format is valid (if .toon file)
  3. Check links work (if markdown with links)
  4. No syntax errors
  5. File is readable and makes sense
danger: Don't commit broken files

[STEP_7_GIT_COMMIT]
task: Commit the documentation change
format:
  git commit -m "docs: [type] brief description

  Source: [where did you find this info?]
  File: [which file updated?]

  Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"

type_options:
  - [constraint] for CONSTRAINTS.toon additions
  - [arch] for ARCHITECTURE.toon changes
  - [project] for PROJECT.toon updates
  - [module] for module-level details
  - [rule] for CLAUDE.md changes
  - [fix] for error corrections
  - [structure] for PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md changes

example_commit:
  git commit -m "docs: [constraint] add FFI validation rule

  Source: code review of bindings/ffi.cpp
  File: docs/agent/CONSTRAINTS.toon

  Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"

[STEP_8_DOCUMENT_SOURCE]
task: Always record where info came from
sources_valid:
  - "User: explicit mention of rule"
  - "Code: line X in file Y (commit hash if known)"
  - "Discovery: code analysis, verified in N locations"
  - "Finding: from code review, present in implementation"
sources_invalid:
  - "Probably from..."
  - "Might be..."
  - "Seems like..."
  - "I assume..."

[COMMON_MISTAKES]
mistake_1: Updating without verifying source
  fix: Check WHEN_TO_UPDATE.toon first

mistake_2: Duplicating existing info
  fix: Search existing docs before adding

mistake_3: Adding speculation or opinion
  fix: Check WHEN_NOT_TO_UPDATE.toon veto list

mistake_4: Huge multi-page update
  fix: Keep updates small (5-10 lines)

mistake_5: Breaking file format/structure
  fix: Read whole file first, understand structure

mistake_6: Forgetting [docs] prefix in commit
  fix: Always use [docs: type] format

mistake_7: No source attribution
  fix: Add "Source: ..." to every commit message

[SUMMARY]
1. Identify (what file? which section?)
2. Locate (where in file?)
3. Check (is it duplicate?)
4. Write (compose update)
5. Edit (use Edit tool)
6. Verify (file is correct?)
7. Commit (with [docs] prefix + source)
8. Document (record where it came from)

Time estimate: 2-5 minutes per update
